      "depth": "brief",
      "title": "The Sigmoid Curve",
      "story": "When modeling growth or decision thresholds, a simple linear scale often fails because real-world systems saturate at extremes. We need a function that maps any input smoothly between zero and one. The logistic sigmoid function provides this smooth transition, taking an input value and compressing it into a bounded range. By adjusting the steepness parameter, we can control how abruptly the transition occurs around the midpoint.",
      "cardDescription": "Explore how the logistic sigmoid curve maps continuous inputs between zero and one. Adjust the steepness parameter to see how it changes the transition around the midpoint.",
      "learningGoal": "Explain why changing steepness preserves the sigmoid bounds.",
      "instructions": "Adjust the steepness slider to change how fast the curve transitions from zero to one. Observe the marker output update in real time.",
